This extension adds Bloodborne modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Automatically downloads and updates shadPS4.[/summary]

[b][color=#ea9999][size=4]Neither the mod author nor Nexus Mods endorse piracy. You must own a legitimate copy of Bloodborne to use this extension.[/size][/color][/b]

Automatically downloads and updates shadPS4.
[b][url=https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadPS4/releases][size=4]Get shadPS4[/size][/url]   &lt;- You may need to download and run separately once to install the Bloodborne game data from a package file, if not already extracted. [/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]ShadPS4 mods with a "shadps4.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]ShadPS4 Qt Launcher installs to the game folder, recognised by a "shadps4qtlauncher.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Smithbox installs to the game folder, recognised by a "smithbox.exe" file.[/*]
[*]FLVER Editor installs to the game folder, recognised by a "flver_editor.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Game Data (dvdroot_ps4) mods with an "action", "chr", "event", "facegen", "map", "menu" or one of 13 other named folders install to the "CUSA03173\dvdroot_ps4" folder.[/*]
[*]Save mods with a "userdata0000" file install to the "user\savedata\1\CUSA03173\SPRJ0005" folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatically downloads and installs a dedicated instance of shadPS4 and the Qt Launcher in the same folder where you have the "CUSA03173" folder. The extension will also check for and download new stable shadPS4 releases.[/*]
[*]Automatically installs mods intended for the game data folder (has a folder that goes inside the "dvdroot_ps4" folder in the mod zip).[/*]
[*]Automatically installs save game file mods to the correct folder ("user&#92;savedata").[/*]
[*]Includes a default tool to launch Bloodborne directly in shadPS4 from Vortex with one click.[/*]
[*]Includes a tool and installer for [url=https://github.com/vawser/Smithbox]Smithbox [/url]﻿modding program (currently gives an error when trying to launch from Vortex).[/*]
[*]Includes a tool and installer for [url=https://github.com/Pear0533/FLVER_Editor]Flver Editor[/url]﻿.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff00][size=3]If you want to launch through the Qt Launcher GUI[/size][/color][/b], set the Qt Launcher tool as the default launch method in the Dashboard tab as shown below.[/*]
[*]The default behavior of the the Vortex launch button is to launch Bloodborne directly through CLI, not through the GUI.[/*]
[*]NOTE: You can get new versions of the Qt Launcher using the button shown below.[/*]
[/list]

[b][color=#b6d7a8][size=4][u]Why use this?:[/u][/size][/color][/b]
[list]
[*][size=3][b][color=#ffff00]Get automatic updates to shadPS4 from GitHub as soon as new stable versions are released! [/color]You will receive a notification in Vortex after running an update check with a button to download the newly-released stable version of shadPS4.[/b][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][b]Allows you to install mods to the Bloodborne game data and save folders without worrying about making manual backups. [/b][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][b]Check for mod updates and download them easily. [/b][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][b]Launch Bloodborne in shadPS4 with a single click from Vortex.[/b][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][b]Easily install experimental versions of shadPS4 by dropping the zip as a mod into Vortex. Your config file will be carried over between versions. [/b][/size][/*]
[*][color=#f9cb9c][size=3][b]Made by an extension author who has made over 220 Vortex Extensions (more than anyone else, ever).[/b][/size][/color][/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4][u]INSTALLATION:[/u][/size][/b]
[list]
[*][size=3][b][color=#ffff00]You must have a "CUSA03173" folder with the extracted game files already in place before using this extension (See below if your folder name is different). [/color][/b]This means you may have to download and run shadPS4 separately (link above) once to unpack and install the Bloodborne game data from the package file. Once you have the game data extracted, you can proceed. [b][color=#f9cb9c]Make sure your Windows user account has write access to the folder where you've placed the game files. This is required for Vortex to be able to install your mods.[/color][/b][/size][/*]
[*][size=3]Download the mod zip and drag and drop it into the drop box in the bottom-right corner of the Vortex "Extensions" tab to install. You must then restart Vortex to complete the installation. [b][color=#ea9999]DO NOT UNPACK THE ZIP ARCHIVE[/color][/b]. Drop the zip file in directly. You may delete the zip once installed to Vortex. [img]https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/55099794810_9b9d8c2378_b.jpg[/img][/size][/*]
[*][size=3]Add Bloodborne in the Vortex "Games" tab. You can use the search box. [/size][/*]
[*][size=3]Select the folder where the "CUSA03173" folder is located when asked to specify the game install location manually. Note that this is a Windows folder select dialogue, so you will not see individual files when selecting the installation directory. You will only see folders. [/size][/*]
[*][size=3]The Vortex extension will download the latest versions of shadPS4 and the Qt Launcher from Github to the same folder containing the "CUSA03173" folder. Note that Vortex needs at least one version of shadPS4 installed through Vortex, or it will attempt to download the latest version again. [/size][/*]
[*][size=3]Have fun modding the game![/size][/*]
[/list]
[color=#ffff00][size=4][b]** If you have a different version of the game other than CUSA03173 **[/b][/size][/color]
[b]You must edit the "PS_ID" variable in the "index.js" file to match your folder name. You can edit the file before installing to Vortex, or after installation at the default plugin location:[/b]
[b]%APPDATA%&#92;Vortex&#92;plugins[/b]
[size=2]You can copy and paste the above address directly into File Explorer.[/size]
[b]The folder name containing the index.js file will be "Bloodborne Vortex Extension" plus some numbers. You can copy the path above directly into the File Explorer bar to open the folder.[/b]
[size=2]Open the index.js file with a text editor (like VS Code or notepad++) and change the variable called "PS_ID" to your game version.
For example, CUSA00900.
[code]﻿const PS_ID = "CUSA03173";[/code][size=2]
becomes:[/size]
[code]const PS_ID = "CUSA00900";[/code][/size]

